044025             0846*   ;
044025             0847*   ; IMPORTANT: umul24 discards product bits above bit 23. That theoretical limit
044025             0848*   ; is 16,777,215 bytes/pixels--orders of magnitude larger than any conceivable
044025             0849*   ; bitmap on the Agon. The initial image loader therefore deliberately uses the
044025             0850*   ; smaller native-ADL result instead of carrying a general u16*u16=u32 routine.
044025             0851*   agnb_calculate_image_data_size:
044025             0852*   ; Load each contiguous u16 field as UHL, then use the established eZ80 idiom
044025             0853*   ; to discard the accidentally loaded following byte.
